diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 19e1dddf4d133f0c6843c9902bcd5bac468a3e67..ae396c0bf9475c7d37a0f81983247be3846a0ba1 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -12,6 +12,26 @@ JavaScript (JS) is a lightweight, interpreted, or just-in-time compiled programm
 
 This implementation uses an explicit MVC pattern, with a clear file structure to reflect the architecture. The storage solution uses an in-memory data object that implements a simple array to hold the todos.
 
+## Undo clear completed
+
+After **Clear completed** removes one or more tasks, **Undo clear completed** becomes available above the footer. It remains available when the task list is empty. Undo restores the latest nonempty batch once, including the original IDs, titles, completion states and order among the original surviving tasks. Tasks added afterward stay at the end of the list; saved edits and completion changes to surviving tasks are preserved. Individually deleted tasks remain deleted.
+
+Another nonempty clear replaces the previous undo batch. An empty clear keeps the pending batch, and undo consumes it. The current All, Active or Completed filter still applies to restored tasks. Both tasks and undo history live only in page memory; reloading starts a fresh list. No localStorage, sessionStorage or other cross-refresh persistence is added.
+
+The Store owns the batch and its original ID order, merges restoration with the current records, and shares that in-memory state between instances with the same store name. The Model exposes those operations; the Controller refreshes the active filter and counts; the View controls the button. The separate undo row keeps the existing empty-list and footer behavior. The build script copies its CSS from `src` along with the existing app files.
+
+## Tests
+
+The tests use Node's built-in test runner and the environment-provided `jsdom` module. They run the actual app scripts and DOM events without a server or network access; no extra dependencies need to be installed in this prepared workspace.
+
+```
+npm test
+npm run build
+TODO_APP_ROOT=dist npm test
+```
+
+Coverage includes exact restoration and ordering, subsequent edits/additions/deletions, empty-list access, repeated clears and undo, all three filters, counts, existing editing/toggle behavior, and page-only storage. The final command repeats the same DOM checks against the generated build and resolves its local CSS and script paths.
+
 ## Build Steps
 
 A simple build script copies all necessary files to a `dist` folder.
